---
import config from '../config';
import Frame from '../layouts/frame.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import ProfileCard from '../widgets/ProfileCard.astro';
import RecentPosts from '../widgets/RecentPosts.astro';
import WebsiteStatus from '../widgets/WebsiteStatus.astro';
---

<Frame
  isHome={true}
  title={config.title}
  breadcrumbs={[{ text: 'Home', href: '/' }]}
>
  <ProfileCard slot="left-header" />
  <RecentPosts slot="left" />
  <WebsiteStatus slot="left" />

  <Prose>
    <h1 class="page-title">✍️ Welcome to My Blog</h1>
    <p>
      Hello there! I am <strong>Kani Nayuta</strong> (可児 那由多) — you can call
      me Nayu, or Kanikou if you're feeling cheeky.
    </p>
    <p>
      By trade, I am a light novel author publishing under <em>GF Bunko</em>.
      Ever since winning the 14th GF Newcomer Award at age 18 with my debut
      novel,
      <em>The Silvery Landscape</em> (銀色景色), critics and readers have called me
      a "literary prodigy." But honestly? I don't calculate plot structures or follow
      textbook storytelling formulas. When inspiration strikes, the scenery simply
      floods into my skull, and my fingers move on their own like a runaway train.
    </p>

    <h2>The Light in the Dark</h2>
    <p>
      During my middle school years, relentless bullying crushed me completely.
      I stopped attending school, severed all contact with society, and spent
      years cooped up inside a dark room as a shut-in <em>hikikomori</em>. I had
      lost the will to exist.
    </p>
    <p>
      The thing that saved my life wasn't words of sympathy or therapy — it was
      picking up the debut novel of an unknown author named <strong
        >Itsuki Hashima</strong
      >. His passion, raw vulnerability, and sheer love for creation rekindled a
      blazing fire inside my hollow chest. From that instant onwards, my
      fundamental operating principle in life has been <strong
        >100% love for Itsuki-senpai</strong
      >. He is my savior, my eternal muse, and my beloved.
    </p>

    <h2>On Writing and Sensations</h2>
    <p>
      People often ask about my creative habits. Here is the unvarnished truth:
      <strong>clothing is the ultimate enemy of artistic expression</strong>.
      Constrictive fabric chokes imagination and cuts off blood flow to the
      brain! When I sit before my keyboard, I cast off every piece of clothing
      and let the cold air touch bare skin. If you ever drop by my apartment
      while a manuscript deadline is ticking down, don't be shocked — just leave
      some food by the door. My poor editor, Toki-san, has had to make peace
      with this eccentricity long ago.
    </p>

    <h2>About This Blog</h2>
    <p>
      This blog is my personal playground and unfiltered digital notebook. Here
      you won't find polite PR statements or corporate press releases — instead,
      I share essays on creative flow, behind-the-scenes thoughts on <em
        >The Landscape Series</em
      >
      (『景色』シリーズ), midnight musings, and stories about the people I love.
    </p>
    <p>
      Take a look through my <a href="/posts">Posts</a>, or meet the precious
      people in my life on the <a href="/friend">Inner Circle</a> page.
    </p>
  </Prose>
</Frame>
